WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.760
Every November, Delhi seems to
disappear under a blanket of pollution.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:04.660
But why?

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.320
It's not just stubble burning.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.390
Delhi already has pollution
from vehicles, industries,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.570
construction dust and other sources.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:12.820
When winter arrives,

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.330
wind speeds often decrease and the
atmosphere becomes less effective at

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.320
dispersing pollutants.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.030
Temperature inversion can trap
polluted air closer to the ground.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:25.220
Add seasonal crop-residue burning, and the
pollution problem can become much worse.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.800
That's why Delhi's air can turn
dangerously unhealthy during winter.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.570
Is Delhi's pollution mainly
caused by stubble burning,

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.350
or is the problem much bigger?

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.260
Tell us below.

